<<<
-B-, -BB-. Monosyllables ending in b double it before suffixes beginning with vowels if the sound preceding it is a single vowel (a, e, i, 0, u, or y), but not if it is a diphthong or a vowel & r: cabby, webbed, glibbest, bobbed, shrubbery; but dauber, barbed.
===
**-B-, -BB-.** Monosyllables ending in b double it before suffixes beginning with vowels if the sound preceding it is a single vowel (a, e, i, o, u, or y), but not if it is a diphthong or a vowel & r: *cabby, webbed, glibbest, bobbed, shrubbery*; but *dauber, barbed*.
>>>

<<<
Words of more syllables (e.g. rhubarb, sillabub, hubbub, Beelzebub, cherub) are few, & it will suffice to mention cherubic (so spelt), & hobnob (-bbed, -bbing).
===
Words of more syllables (e.g. *rhubarb, sillabub, hubbub, Beelzebub, cherub*) are few, & it will suffice to mention *cherubic* (so spelt), & *hobnob (-bbed, -bbing)*.
>>>

